\b DebloatManager \b0 \line
Terms of Use, Disclaimer, and Privacy Notice\line
\line
\b 1. What this software does\b0\line
DebloatManager scans this device for preinstalled Windows apps, optional system features, and background services, and lets you end their running tasks or remove them. Some actions target core Windows components.\line
\line
\b 2. No warranty\b0\line
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Removing system components or Windows optional features can make Windows behave unexpectedly or break other applications. You are solely responsible for reviewing each item's risk level and for any consequences of removing it.\line
\line
\b 3. Recommended precautions\b0\line
Use the built-in "Create Restore Point" option before performing risky actions, so changes can be undone through Windows System Restore if needed.\line
\line
\b 4. Privacy\b0\line
DebloatManager does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data to any server. It does not use analytics, telemetry, or network connections of its own. All scanning and removal actions run entirely on this device using local Windows APIs (registry, PowerShell, WMI). An activity log is written only to this device, under %LocalAppData%\\DebloatManager\\logs, for your own troubleshooting reference.\line
\line
\b 5. Acceptance\b0\line
By clicking Install, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this notice and accept these risks.\line
